{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And his sons carried him.</b> And not his sons' sons — for so he charged them: let no Egyptian man carry my bier, nor any of your sons, for they are of the daughters of Canaan, but you. And he fixed for them a place, three to the east, and likewise for the four directions, and in their order of the camp of standards they were fixed here. Levi would not carry, for he is destined to carry the ark; and Joseph would not carry, because he is a king; Manasseh and Ephraim would be under them. And this is ״אִישׁ עַל דִּגְלוֹ בְּאֹתֹת״ — by the sign that their father transmitted to them for carrying his bier."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 50, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:04:26.558492238Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}